  <slide>
    <title>Let a script do it</title>
    <p><alert>How it’s coded · Skeletal notes · step 4 of 4.</alert> The Posting Desk makes that edit with a script: find the wrapped include, put the bare include back, then validate and commit.</p>
    <p>From <c>M13-Mehdi/scripts/desk_action.py</c></p>
    <program language="python" highlight-lines="3-4,13">
<code>
def wrapped_re(href):
    return re.compile(
        r'&lt;!--\s*UNPOSTED(?:-WITH topic="([^"]*)")?\s+'
        r'(&lt;xi:include\s+href="\.?/?%s"\s*/&gt;)\s+UNPOSTED\s*--&gt;' % re.escape(href)
    )
…
def post_include(path, href):
    """Unwrap one include.  Returns 'done', 'already', or 'absent'."""
    text = read(path)
    m = wrapped_re(href).search(text)
    if m is None:
        return "already" if inc_re(href).search(text) else "absent"
    write(path, text[: m.start()] + m.group(2) + text[m.end():])
    return "done"
</code>
</program>
  </slide>

